      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm not entirely sure how much of a performance benefit this would provide for null checks and I would need to profile it. Similar for JUMP_IF_ZERO. The tradeoff for both is that they need to determine the type they are comparing; `int` comparison is not the same as `float` comparison, and similarly`System.Object` comparison is not the same as `UnityEngine.Object` comparison. So to avoid overhead of checking the argument types they'd each need to be split off into their own instructions. Externs have the benefit in a way that they already have the exact comparison op they need.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62d6416c63174b44b66dafdb",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f94ffe74fcf4c0e78f6111f",
        "alias": "International orange Sturgeon",
        "aliasID": "65c4b368ed6eefce4c294168",
