      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So basically a suite of numerical comparison operations, paired with types\n{beq,bne,blt,bge}{fi} + {beq,bne}{U,O} - or some subset thereof*.\n* branch if equal/branch if not equal/branch if less than/branch if greater than or equal\nIt might be worth either examining the UASM output of commonplace/popular prefabs (anyone could do this), and counting the number of equality extern calls to estimate the impact of such instructions.\nThis would somewhat resemble a move from RISC to CISC, but given that the Udon VM is a straight-up interpreter and not a JIT it sort of makes sense to ahead-of-time optimize with specialized instructions.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
