      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61898ae3ee3a174b8e9086e5|full_name}: Fair enough.\nWhat if the ops were combined into a JUMP_IF_INEQUAL? would the == operation be a valid case for moving into UASM land? For the UnityEngine.Object, it's already recommended to use the Utilities.IsValid anyways, so the JUMP_IF_FALSE op would apply for that one.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
